{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1523004-boosting-the-roll-speed","id":1523004,"title":"Boosting the roll speed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-09-23T03:34:49-07:00","id":1523004,"title":"Boosting the roll speed","content":"The main issue of some of my friends when we've began to play W20 and V20 was the excessive number of rolls, to activate a power, soak, damage and so on, especially during the fighting. With time and test i've created house rules to speed up high number of roll, their success with my friend made me think it would be helpful for other player so i share 2 of them here<br /> <br /> 1) Powerful Roll is used when the dice pool of a pc or npc is higher than 10, in the case of a vampire with potence or celerity, a werewolf in another form, or someone making a full auto shoot with his riffle. With that rule yoy never roll more than 10 dice but you add on your result the last point of you roll, i explain:<br /> <br /> You play a vampire with Dex 5 firearms 5 and celerity 5, that would make you roll 15 dice with the basic rule. Here you roll only 10 and add the last 5 point to the success you've roll, but only enough to double your roll result. If after rolling your 10 dice you've got 3 success you can only add 3 ou your 5 last point to obtain a final result of 6 success. If you rolled 5 success or more with you roll then you can add all your 5 final points.<br /> <br /> The result can be doubled when you have 11 to 20 dice in your pool, so basically if you have 20 dice just double any success on you roll. But what happen if your vampire make a full auto and get to 25 dice to roll? Then you double the success you've obtained and add the 5 last point to triple youre success. If after rolling your 10 dice you get 3 success you double it and add 3 more to get a final result of 9 success.<br /> <br /> A pool from 11 to 20 allow you to double the success rolled, a pool of 21 to 30 allow you to triple them, a pool of 31 to 40 allow you to quadruple them and so on.<br /> <br /> With that rule even on your physical table with your friend you only need 10 dice to play and you roll only one time even with very large dice pool<br /> <br /> 2) The Automatic Roll is use to skip some roll (soak, damage and even powers if the st agree). To make it work you just take half of you pool and use it as you final result when the difficulty is 6. If the difficulty is higher substract 1 die AFTER taking half of you pool. Let's say you have 10 dice, on a difficulty 6 your automatic roll give you 5 success, on a difficulty 7 it give you 4, on a difficulty 8 it give you 3 and so on.<br /> When the difficulty is below 6 you get one die from the other half of you pool. That way on a very low difficulty you can never obtain more success than you basic pool. A difficulty 5 give you back 1 die, a difficulty 4 give you back 2 dice and so on.<br /> If you have a specialty you can add 1 more die to you Automatic Roll AFTER halving it and BEFORE adjusting with the difficulty.<br /> <br /> The Automatic Roll rule does not work if you roll more than 10 dice, that rule depend on the Powerfull Roll rule to work properly<br /> <br /> Those 2 rule saved us a huge amount of time especially during combat where i could as a st make the ennemy roll in automatic according to their pool and their action, so only the pc would roll and &quot;skip&quot; the soaking and damage part to concentrate only on their actions.<br /> <br /> Disclaimer: These are House Rules that work perfectly with OUR game, i'm sharing them hoping other players can find in them a solution to speed up their game. I'm not saying they're perfect or anything but they worked well enough for us to make me think they could be useful for others","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 09-23-2023, 07:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}